Option: clean-addresses-C
Name: Page addresses without .html (Cloudflare Pages)
Does: Sets PAGE_EXT = "" in tools/pages.py, so the extra pages name themselves to Google as /wise-pie, not /wise-pie.html (canonical tag, share address, structured data, sitemap). Cloudflare Pages redirects /wise-pie.html to /wise-pie, so without this the canonical tags point at an address that redirects. Updates the public-site test (a sitemap address may omit .html) and the README and checklist wording. Links inside the site keep .html. The validity test accepts the sitemap addresses without .html (they name the page file with .html). It also teaches tests/launch-check.test.mjs the address style (PAGE_EXT) and a host that opens /x from x.html, so the launch-check test passes with this patch applied, and splits one 46-word sentence of the checklist in two (plain-lint was red with this patch: its [hold] line in tools/plain_words.txt no longer matched the rewritten sentence, which now starts with the held words again). The seo test reads PAGE_EXT itself (a fix in the base: job w205).
